{"id":"gma-fig-005","s":"maths","t":"A11-A12","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows a cubic curve. For which values of $k$ does the horizontal line $y=k$ cross the curve at exactly three points?","o":["$-1<k<1$","$k<-2$ or $k>2$","$k=-2$ or $k=2$","$-2<k<2$"],"a":3,"x":"The turning points are at $(-1,2)$ and $(1,-2)$. A horizontal line cuts the curve three times only when it lies between those heights, so $-2<k<2$.","w":["Used the $x$-values of the turning points, $-1$ and $1$, instead of their $y$-values.","Picked the values where the line meets the curve only once. These are outside the turning points.","Used the $y$-values of the turning points. A line there touches the curve at only two points.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-3,3],"y":[-4,4],"xstep":1,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-3.0,-18.0],[-2.9625,-17.112604],[-2.925,-16.250203],[-2.8875,-15.412482],[-2.85,-14.599125],[-2.8125,-13.809814],[-2.775,-13.044234],[-2.7375,-12.302068],[-2.7,-11.583],[-2.6625,-10.886713],[-2.625,-10.212891],[-2.5875,-9.561217],[-2.55,-8.931375],[-2.5125,-8.323049],[-2.475,-7.735922],[-2.4375,-7.169678],[-2.4,-6.624],[-2.3625,-6.098572],[-2.325,-5.593078],[-2.2875,-5.107201],[-2.25,-4.640625],[-2.2125,-4.193033],[-2.175,-3.764109],[-2.1375,-3.353537],[-2.1,-2.961],[-2.0625,-2.586182],[-2.025,-2.228766],[-1.9875,-1.888436],[-1.95,-1.564875],[-1.9125,-1.257768],[-1.875,-0.966797],[-1.8375,-0.691646],[-1.8,-0.432],[-1.7625,-0.187541],[-1.725,0.042047],[-1.6875,0.25708],[-1.65,0.457875],[-1.6125,0.644748],[-1.575,0.818016],[-1.5375,0.977994],[-1.5,1.125],[-1.4625,1.25935],[-1.425,1.381359],[-1.3875,1.491346],[-1.35,1.589625],[-1.3125,1.676514],[-1.275,1.752328],[-1.2375,1.817385],[-1.2,1.872],[-1.1625,1.91649],[-1.125,1.951172],[-1.0875,1.976361],[-1.05,1.992375],[-1.0125,1.999529],[-0.975,1.998141],[-0.9375,1.988525],[-0.9,1.971],[-0.8625,1.945881],[-0.825,1.913484],[-0.7875,1.874127],[-0.75,1.828125],[-0.7125,1.775795],[-0.675,1.717453],[-0.6375,1.653416],[-0.6,1.584],[