{"id":"gma-fig-016","s":"maths","t":"A11-A12","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows a cubic curve. Which equation matches the curve?","o":["$y=(x-1)(x+1)(x+2)$","$y=-(x+1)(x-1)(x-2)$","$y=-(x-1)(x+1)(x+2)$","$y=(x+1)(x-1)(x-2)$"],"a":3,"x":"The curve crosses the $x$-axis at $-1$, $1$ and $2$. So the factors are $(x+1)$, $(x-1)$ and $(x-2)$. The curve rises on the right, so there is no minus sign. Check at $x=0$: $(1)(-1)(-2)=2$, as on the graph.","w":["Wrote the root $x=2$ as $(x+2)$. The factor for a root $x=2$ is $(x-2)$.","Used the right factors but put a minus sign in front. That would make the curve fall on the right, which it does not.","Made two slips: the factor for the root at 2 has the wrong sign, and the curve was turned upside down.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-2,3],"y":[-12,12],"xstep":1,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-2.0,-12.0],[-1.96875,-11.414032],[-1.9375,-10.843506],[-1.90625,-10.288239],[-1.875,-9.748047],[-1.84375,-9.222748],[-1.8125,-8.712158],[-1.78125,-8.216095],[-1.75,-7.734375],[-1.71875,-7.266815],[-1.6875,-6.813232],[-1.65625,-6.373444],[-1.625,-5.947266],[-1.59375,-5.534515],[-1.5625,-5.13501],[-1.53125,-4.748566],[-1.5,-4.375],[-1.46875,-4.01413],[-1.4375,-3.665771],[-1.40625,-3.329742],[-1.375,-3.005859],[-1.34375,-2.693939],[-1.3125,-2.393799],[-1.28125,-2.105255],[-1.25,-1.828125],[-1.21875,-1.562225],[-1.1875,-1.307373],[-1.15625,-1.063385],[-1.125,-0.830078],[-1.09375,-0.607269],[-1.0625,-0.394775],[-1.03125,-0.192413],[-1.0,0.0],[-0.96875,0.182648],[-0.9375,0.355713],[-0.90625,0.519379],[-0.875,0.673828],[-0.84375,0.819244],[-0.8125,0.955811],[-0.78125,1.08371],[-0.75,1.203125],[-0.71875,1.31424],[-0.6875,1.417236],[-0.65625,1.512299],[-0.625,1.599609],[-0.59375,1.679352],[-0.5625,1.751709],[-0.53125,1.816864],[-0.5,1.875],[-0.46875,1.9263],[-0.4375,1.970947],[-0.40625,2.009125],[-0.375,2.041016],[-0.34375,2.066803],[-0.3125,2.08667],[-0.28125,2.1008],[-0.25,2.109375],[-0.21875,2.112579],[-0.1875,2.110596],[-0.156