{"id":"gma-fig-039","s":"maths","t":"R15","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows a runner's distance from the start. A tangent is drawn at point P. Use the tangent to estimate the runner's speed at P.","o":["2 m/s","4 m/s","8 m/s","0.25 m/s"],"a":1,"x":"Read two points on the tangent: (2, 0) and (6, 16). The gradient is $\\frac{16-0}{6-2}=4$. The speed at P is about 4 m/s.","w":["Divides the distance at P by the time at P (8 ÷ 4). That is the gradient of a line from the origin, not of the tangent.","","Reads the distance at P off the vertical axis and uses it as the speed.","Turns the gradient upside down by working out change in time divided by change in distance."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,8],"y":[0,32],"xstep":1,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"distance / m","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.05,0.00125],[0.1,0.005],[0.15,0.01125],[0.2,0.02],[0.25,0.03125],[0.3,0.045],[0.35,0.06125],[0.4,0.08],[0.45,0.10125],[0.5,0.125],[0.55,0.15125],[0.6,0.18],[0.65,0.21125],[0.7,0.245],[0.75,0.28125],[0.8,0.32],[0.85,0.36125],[0.9,0.405],[0.95,0.45125],[1.0,0.5],[1.05,0.55125],[1.1,0.605],[1.15,0.66125],[1.2,0.72],[1.25,0.78125],[1.3,0.845],[1.35,0.91125],[1.4,0.98],[1.45,1.05125],[1.5,1.125],[1.55,1.20125],[1.6,1.28],[1.65,1.36125],[1.7,1.445],[1.75,1.53125],[1.8,1.62],[1.85,1.71125],[1.9,1.805],[1.95,1.90125],[2.0,2.0],[2.05,2.10125],[2.1,2.205],[2.15,2.31125],[2.2,2.42],[2.25,2.53125],[2.3,2.645],[2.35,2.76125],[2.4,2.88],[2.45,3.00125],[2.5,3.125],[2.55,3.25125],[2.6,3.38],[2.65,3.51125],[2.7,3.645],[2.75,3.78125],[2.8,3.92],[2.85,4.06125],[2.9,4.205],[2.95,4.35125],[3.0,4.5],[3.05,4.65125],[3.1,4.805],[3.15,4.96125],[3.2,5.12],[3.25,5.28125],[3.3,5.445],[3.35,5.61125],[3.4,5.78],[3.45,5.95125],[3.5,6.125],[3.55,6.30125],[3.6,6.48],[3.65,6.66125],[3.7,6.845],[3.75,7.03125],[3.8,7.22],[3.85,7.41125],[3.9,7.605],[3.95,7.80125],[4.0,8.0],[4.05,8.20125],[4.1,8.405],[4.15,8.61125],[4.2,8.82],[4.25,9.03125],[4.3,9.245],[4.35,9.46125],[4.4,9.68],[4.45,9.90125],[4.5,10.125],[4.55,10.35