{"id":"gma-fig-040","s":"maths","t":"R15","lv":3,"q":"Water drains from a tank. The graph shows the volume of water, with a tangent drawn at P. Which statement about the rate of change at P is correct?","o":["Falling at 12 litres per second","Rising at 0.2 litres per second","Falling at 0.2 litres per second","Falling at 720 litres per second"],"a":2,"x":"The tangent passes through (2, 60) and (7, 0). Gradient $=\\frac{0-60}{7-2}=-12$ litres per minute. Divide by 60 to get seconds: falling at 0.2 litres per second.","w":["Finds the gradient correctly but leaves it in litres per minute, so the time unit is wrong.","Ignores the negative gradient. The tangent slopes down, so the volume is falling, not rising.","","Multiplies by 60 instead of dividing when changing litres per minute to litres per second."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,9],"y":[0,100],"xstep":1,"ystep":20,"xlabel":"time / minutes","ylabel":"volume / litres","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,100.0],[0.05625,98.878164],[0.1125,97.762656],[0.16875,96.653477],[0.225,95.550625],[0.28125,94.454102],[0.3375,93.363906],[0.39375,92.280039],[0.45,91.2025],[0.50625,90.131289],[0.5625,89.066406],[0.61875,88.007852],[0.675,86.955625],[0.73125,85.909727],[0.7875,84.870156],[0.84375,83.836914],[0.9,82.81],[0.95625,81.789414],[1.0125,80.775156],[1.06875,79.767227],[1.125,78.765625],[1.18125,77.770352],[1.2375,76.781406],[1.29375,75.798789],[1.35,74.8225],[1.40625,73.852539],[1.4625,72.888906],[1.51875,71.931602],[1.575,70.980625],[1.63125,70.035977],[1.6875,69.097656],[1.74375,68.165664],[1.8,67.24],[1.85625,66.320664],[1.9125,65.407656],[1.96875,64.500977],[2.025,63.600625],[2.08125,62.706602],[2.1375,61.818906],[2.19375,60.937539],[2.25,60.0625],[2.30625,59.193789],[2.3625,58.331406],[2.41875,57.475352],[2.475,56.625625],[2.53125,55.782227],[2.5875,54.945156],[2.64375,54.114414],[2.7,53.29],[2.75625,52.471914],[2.8125,51.660156],[2.86875,50.854727],[2.925,50.055625],[2.98125,49.262852],[3.0375,48.476406],[3.09375,47.696289],[3.15,