{"id":"gma-fig-023","s":"maths","t":"A16","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows a circle with centre $O$ and a point $P$ on the circle. Which of these is the equation of the tangent to the circle at $P$?","o":["$y=-\\frac{1}{2}x$","$y=2x+10$","$y=2x-6$","$y=-2x-6$"],"a":1,"x":"Read $P=(-4,2)$. The radius gradient is $\\frac{2}{-4}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, so the tangent gradient is $2$. Then $y-2=2(x+4)$ gives $y=2x+10$.","w":["You gave the line through $O$ and $P$. That is the radius, not the tangent.","","You used $y-2=2(x-4)$. Since $P$ has $x=-4$, the bracket should be $(x+4)$.","You used $-2$. The gradient perpendicular to $-\\frac{1}{2}$ is $+2$, so the sign is wrong."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-6,6],"y":[-6,6],"xstep":2,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[4.472136,0.0],[4.469412,0.156075],[4.461242,0.31196],[4.447637,0.467465],[4.428613,0.622401],[4.404194,0.776578],[4.374409,0.929809],[4.339294,1.081908],[4.298893,1.232688],[4.253254,1.381966],[4.202433,1.529561],[4.146492,1.675292],[4.085499,1.818982],[4.019529,1.960455],[3.948662,2.099541],[3.872983,2.236068],[3.792586,2.369871],[3.707569,2.500787],[3.618034,2.628656],[3.524091,2.753322],[3.425855,2.874634],[3.323445,2.992443],[3.216985,3.106607],[3.106607,3.216985],[2.992443,3.323445],[2.874634,3.425855],[2.753322,3.524091],[2.628656,3.618034],[2.500787,3.707569],[2.369871,3.792586],[2.236068,3.872983],[2.099541,3.948662],[1.960455,4.019529],[1.818982,4.085499],[1.675292,4.146492],[1.529561,4.202433],[1.381966,4.253254],[1.232688,4.298893],[1.081908,4.339294],[0.929809,4.374409],[0.776578,4.404194],[0.622401,4.428613],[0.467465,4.447637],[0.31196,4.461242],[0.156075,4.469412],[0.0,4.472136],[-0.156075,4.469412],[-0.31196,4.461242],[-0.467465,4.447637],[-0.622401,4.428613],[-0.776578,4.404194],[-0.929809,4.374409],[-1.081908,4.339294],[-1.232688,4.298893],[-1.381966,4.253254],[-1.529561,4.202433],[-1.675292,4.146492],[-1.818982,4.085499],[-1.960455,4.019529],[-2.099541,3.948662],[-2.236068,3.872983],[-2.3