{"id":"gma-fig-019","s":"maths","t":"A13","lv":3,"q":"Curve A is the graph of $y=f(x)$, where $f(x)=x^2$. Curve B is a reflection and a translation of curve A. Use the graph to decide which equation gives curve B.","o":["$y=-f(x+1)+4$","$y=-f(x-1)+4$","$y=-f(x-1)-4$","$y=f(x-1)+4$"],"a":1,"x":"B is upside down, so there is a minus sign outside: $-f(x)$. Its turning point is $(1,4)$, so it moved 1 right and 4 up. That gives $y=-f(x-1)+4$.","w":["Read the shift as 1 left. $f(x+1)$ moves the graph left, but B's turning point is at $x=1$, to the right.","","Got the 4 the wrong way round. B's maximum is at $y=4$, which is 4 up, so the 4 is added.","Ignored that B is upside down. Without the minus sign outside, the curve would still have a minimum."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-2,3],"y":[-6,10],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-2.0,4.0],[-1.96875,3.875977],[-1.9375,3.753906],[-1.90625,3.633789],[-1.875,3.515625],[-1.84375,3.399414],[-1.8125,3.285156],[-1.78125,3.172852],[-1.75,3.0625],[-1.71875,2.954102],[-1.6875,2.847656],[-1.65625,2.743164],[-1.625,2.640625],[-1.59375,2.540039],[-1.5625,2.441406],[-1.53125,2.344727],[-1.5,2.25],[-1.46875,2.157227],[-1.4375,2.066406],[-1.40625,1.977539],[-1.375,1.890625],[-1.34375,1.805664],[-1.3125,1.722656],[-1.28125,1.641602],[-1.25,1.5625],[-1.21875,1.485352],[-1.1875,1.410156],[-1.15625,1.336914],[-1.125,1.265625],[-1.09375,1.196289],[-1.0625,1.128906],[-1.03125,1.063477],[-1.0,1.0],[-0.96875,0.938477],[-0.9375,0.878906],[-0.90625,0.821289],[-0.875,0.765625],[-0.84375,0.711914],[-0.8125,0.660156],[-0.78125,0.610352],[-0.75,0.5625],[-0.71875,0.516602],[-0.6875,0.472656],[-0.65625,0.430664],[-0.625,0.390625],[-0.59375,0.352539],[-0.5625,0.316406],[-0.53125,0.282227],[-0.5,0.25],[-0.46875,0.219727],[-0.4375,0.191406],[-0.40625,0.165039],[-0.375,0.140625],[-0.34375,0.118164],[-0.3125,0.097656],[-0.28125,0.079102],[-0.25,0.0625],[-0.21875,0.047852],[-0.1875,0.035156],[-0.15625,0.024414],[-0.125,0.015625],[-