{"id":"gma-fig-048","s":"maths","t":"S3","lv":3,"q":"The histogram shows waiting times. Assume the times are spread evenly within each bar. Use the graph to estimate how many people waited more than 20 minutes.","o":["50","20","35","15"],"a":2,"x":"Frequency = frequency density × class width. From 20 to 25 the height is 3, so 5 × 3 = 15. The bar from 25 to 45 has height 1, so 20 × 1 = 20. Total 35.","w":["Counted the whole bar from 15 to 25 instead of only the part above 20.","Used only the last bar and left out the part of the 15 to 25 bar above 20.","","Counted only the part from 20 to 25 and left out the last bar."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,45],"y":[0,5],"xstep":5,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"waiting time / minutes","ylabel":"frequency density","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[0,2],[10,2],[10,4],[15,4],[15,3],[25,3],[25,1],[45,1],[45,0],[0,0]],"c":0}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gma-fig-049","s":"maths","t":"S3","lv":3,"q":"The cumulative frequency graph shows the journey times of some workers. Use the graph to find the interquartile range.","o":["20 minutes","30 minutes","40 minutes","60 minutes"],"a":0,"x":"The total is 80. The lower quartile is at cumulative frequency 20, which is 20 minutes. The upper quartile is at 60, which is 40 minutes. IQR = 40 − 20 = 20 minutes.","w":["","Read the median (at cumulative frequency 40) instead of finding the difference between the quartiles.","Subtracted the cumulative frequencies 60 and 20 instead of the two times.","Gave the cumulative frequency of the upper quartile, 60, instead of a difference in times."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,60],"y":[0,80],"xstep":10,"ystep":10,"xlabel":"journey time / minutes","ylabel":"cumulative frequency","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[10,10],[20,20],[30,40],[40,60],[50,70],[60,80]],"c":0}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gma-fig-050","s":"maths","t":"S3","lv":3,"q":"The cumulative frequency graph shows test marks for two classes, A and B, with the same number of students. Which statement is correct?","o":["A has a higher median than B, and the same IQR","B has a higher median than A, and a larger IQR","A and B have the same median, because both curves end at the same point","B has a higher median than A, and the same IQR"],"a":3,"x":"Both have 40 students, so the median is at cumulative frequency 20: A is 30, B is 40. Quartiles are at 10 and 30: A gives 20 and 40, B gives 30 and 50. Both IQRs are 20.","w":["Thought the higher curve means higher marks. The curve further to the right has the higher values.","Saw B start later and rise steeply and took that as more spread, but both IQRs are 20.","Saw both curves end at 40 students and did not compare the marks at cumulative frequency 20.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,60],"y":[0,40],"xstep":10,"ystep":5,"xlabel":"test mark","ylabel":"cumulative frequency","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[10,5],[20,10],[30,20],[40,30],[50,35],[60,40]],"label":"A","c":0},{"pts":[[0,0],[20,0],[30,10],[40,20],[50,30],[60,40]],"label":"B","c":1}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gma-fig-051","s":"maths","t":"S3","lv":3,"q":"The histogram shows the ages of people at a club. Which class has the greatest frequency, and what is that frequency?","o":["$10 \\le x < 20$, frequency 5","$20 \\le x < 40$, frequency 60","$20 \\le x < 40$, frequency 3","$10 \\le x < 20$, frequency 50"],"a":1,"x":"Frequency = frequency density × width. Bars: 0–10 gives 4 × 10 = 40. 10–20 gives 5 × 10 = 50. 20–40 gives 3 × 20 = 60. 40–60 gives 1 × 20 = 20. The tallest bar is not the largest.","w":["Picked the tallest bar and gave its height, which is frequency density, not frequency.","","Picked the right class but gave its frequency density, not its frequency.","Picked the tallest bar. Its frequency is 50, but the wider bar has more."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,60],"y":[0,6],"xstep":10,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"age / years","ylabel":"frequency density","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[0,4],[10,4],[10,5],[20,5],[20,3],[40,3],[40,1],[60,1],[60,0],[0,0]],"c":0}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gma-fig-033","s":"maths","t":"R10-R11","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows a cycle ride. What was the cyclist's speed in the last section, after the rest?","o":["22.9 km/h","60 km/h","40 km/h","53.3 km/h"],"a":2,"x":"The last section runs from 2 h to 3.5 h, so it takes 1.5 h. The distance goes from 20 km to 80 km, which is 60 km. Speed = 60 ÷ 1.5 = 40 km/h.","w":["Used the whole ride: total distance divided by total time. The question asks only about the last section.","Used the distance covered, 60 km, as the speed. You must divide by the time taken.","","Used the total distance at the end, 80 km, but only the time of the last section. Use the distance covered in that section."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,4],"y":[0,100],"xstep":0.5,"ystep":20,"xlabel":"time / hours","ylabel":"distance / km","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[1,20],[2,20],[3.5,80]],"c":0}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gma-fig-034","s":"maths","t":"R10-R11","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows mass against volume for two metals, A and B. How much greater is the density of A than the density of B?","o":["3 g/cm³","30 g/cm³","1.6 g/cm³","13 g/cm³"],"a":0,"x":"Density = mass ÷ volume. At 10 cm³, A has mass 80 g, so its density is 8 g/cm³. B has mass 50 g, so its density is 5 g/cm³. The difference is 3 g/cm³.","w":["","Subtracted the two masses at 10 cm³ instead of finding the two densities first.","Divided 8 by 5 to compare the densities. The question asks how much greater, so subtract.","Added the two densities instead of finding the difference."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,10],"y":[0,80],"xstep":2,"ystep":10,"xlabel":"volume / cm³","ylabel":"mass / g","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[10,80]],"label":"A","c":0},{"pts":[[0,0],[10,50]],"label":"B","c":1}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gma-fig-035","s":"maths","t":"R10-R11","lv":2,"q":"A box of fixed weight rests on the floor. The graph shows the pressure it exerts for different base areas. Point P is marked. What is the weight of the box?","o":["43 N","13.3 N","37 N","120 N"],"a":3,"x":"Pressure = force ÷ area, so force = pressure × area. At P the area is 3 m² and the pressure is 40 N/m². Force = 40 × 3 = 120 N. The weight is this force.","w":["Added the area and the pressure from P instead of multiplying them.","Divided the pressure by the area. To find the force, multiply them.","Subtracted the area from the pressure instead of multiplying.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,6],"y":[0,120],"xstep":1,"ystep":20,"xlabel":"area / m²","ylabel":"pressure / N/m²","lines":[{"pts":[[1,120],[1.2,100],[1.5,80],[1.75,68.6],[2,60],[2.4,50],[2.5,48],[3,40],[4,30],[5,24],[6,20]],"c":0}],"points":[{"at":[3,40],"label":"P"}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gma-fig-020","s":"maths","t":"A14-A15","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows Ana and Leo cycling along the same road from home. Leo sets off later. How far from home are they when Leo catches up with Ana?","o":["40 km","20 km","2 km","30 km"],"a":1,"x":"Leo catches Ana where the two lines cross. The lines cross at 2 hours. Read across to the distance axis: 20 km.","w":["Reads Leo's final distance instead of the point where the lines cross.","","Reads the time (2 hours) from the horizontal axis instead of the distance from the vertical axis.","Reads Ana's distance at the time Leo stops, not where the two lines meet."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,5],"y":[0,50],"xstep":1,"ystep":10,"xlabel":"time / hours","ylabel":"distance from home / km","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[5,50]],"label":"Ana","c":0},{"pts":[[0,0],[1,0],[3,40]],"label":"Leo","c":1}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gma-fig-021","s":"maths","t":"A14-A15","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the cost of hiring a bike for different times. Which statement about the hire charges is correct?","o":["Fixed charge £3, then £6 for each hour","Fixed charge £12, then £3 for each hour","Fixed charge £6, then £3 for each hour","Fixed charge £6, then £4 for each hour"],"a":2,"x":"The line starts at £6 on the cost axis, so the fixed charge is £6. Gradient = (24 − 6) ÷ 6 = 3, so each hour costs £3.","w":["Swaps the meanings: takes the gradient as the fixed charge and the intercept as the hourly rate.","Takes the cost at 2 hours as the fixed charge instead of the intercept at 0 hours.","","Divides the cost at 6 hours by 6, which wrongly includes the fixed charge in the hourly rate."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,6],"y":[0,30],"xstep":1,"ystep":6,"xlabel":"time / hours","ylabel":"cost / £","lines":[{"pts":[[0,6],[6,24]],"c":0}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gma-fig-022","s":"maths","t":"A14-A15","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows the speed of a cyclist. Use four trapezia of equal width to estimate the distance travelled in the time shown.","o":["36 m","32 m","40 m","72 m"],"a":0,"x":"Strips are 1 s wide. Speeds at 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 s are 0, 8, 12, 12, 8. Area = ½ × 1 × (0 + 2×8 + 2×12 + 2×12 + 8) = 36 m.","w":["","Uses rectangles with left-hand heights (0, 8, 12, 12) instead of trapezia.","Uses rectangles with right-hand heights (8, 12, 12, 8) instead of trapezia.","Forgets the ½ in the trapezium area, which doubles the answer."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,4],"y":[0,16],"xstep":1,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"speed / m/s","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.025,0.24875],[0.05,0.495],[0.075,0.73875],[0.1,0.98],[0.125,1.21875],[0.15,1.455],[0.175,1.68875],[0.2,1.92],[0.225,2.14875],[0.25,2.375],[0.275,2.59875],[0.3,2.82],[0.325,3.03875],[0.35,3.255],[0.375,3.46875],[0.4,3.68],[0.425,3.88875],[0.45,4.095],[0.475,4.29875],[0.5,4.5],[0.525,4.69875],[0.55,4.895],[0.575,5.08875],[0.6,5.28],[0.625,5.46875],[0.65,5.655],[0.675,5.83875],[0.7,6.02],[0.725,6.19875],[0.75,6.375],[0.775,6.54875],[0.8,6.72],[0.825,6.88875],[0.85,7.055],[0.875,7.21875],[0.9,7.38],[0.925,7.53875],[0.95,7.695],[0.975,7.84875],[1.0,8.0],[1.025,8.14875],[1.05,8.295],[1.075,8.43875],[1.1,8.58],[1.125,8.71875],[1.15,8.855],[1.175,8.98875],[1.2,9.12],[1.225,9.24875],[1.25,9.375],[1.275,9.49875],[1.3,9.62],[1.325,9.73875],[1.35,9.855],[1.375,9.96875],[1.4,10.08],[1.425,10.18875],[1.45,10.295],[1.475,10.39875],[1.5,10.5],[1.525,10.59875],[1.55,10.695],[1.575,10.78875],[1.6,10.88],[1.625,10.96875],[1.65,11.055],[1.675,11.13875],[1.7,11.22],[1.725,11.29875],[1.75,11.375],[1.775,11.44875],[1.8,11.52],[1.825,11.58875],[1.85,11.655],[1.875,11.71875],[1.9,11.78],[1.925,11.83875],[1.95,11.895],[1.975,11.94875],[2.0,12.0],[2.025,12.04875],[2.05,12.095],[2.075,12.13875],[2.1,12.18],[2.125,12.21875],[2.15,12.255],[2.175,12.28875],[2.2,12.32],[2.225,12.34875],[2.25,12.