{"id":"gma-fig-025","s":"maths","t":"A17-A18","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the curve $y=x^2+bx+c$. The curve crosses the x-axis at P and Q. Which equation is the equation of the curve?","o":["$y=x^2+x-6$","$y=x^2-x-6$","$y=x^2-5x+6$","$y=x^2-x+6$"],"a":1,"x":"The curve crosses the x-axis at $x=-2$ and $x=3$. So $y=(x+2)(x-3)=x^2-x-6$. It also crosses the y-axis at $-6$, which matches.","w":["Swapped the signs, using $(x-2)(x+3)$. The roots are $-2$ and $3$, so the factors are $(x+2)$ and $(x-3)$.","","Used the roots as 2 and 3 and lost the minus sign on $-2$. The curve does not cross the x-axis at 2.","Got the factors right but made the constant $+6$. The graph crosses the y-axis at $-6$."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-3,4],"y":[-8,6],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"x","ylabel":"y","lines":[{"pts":[[-3.0,6.0],[-2.95625,5.695664],[-2.9125,5.395156],[-2.86875,5.098477],[-2.825,4.805625],[-2.78125,4.516602],[-2.7375,4.231406],[-2.69375,3.950039],[-2.65,3.6725],[-2.60625,3.398789],[-2.5625,3.128906],[-2.51875,2.862852],[-2.475,2.600625],[-2.43125,2.342227],[-2.3875,2.087656],[-2.34375,1.836914],[-2.3,1.59],[-2.25625,1.346914],[-2.2125,1.107656],[-2.16875,0.872227],[-2.125,0.640625],[-2.08125,0.412852],[-2.0375,0.188906],[-1.99375,-0.031211],[-1.95,-0.2475],[-1.90625,-0.459961],[-1.8625,-0.668594],[-1.81875,-0.873398],[-1.775,-1.074375],[-1.73125,-1.271523],[-1.6875,-1.464844],[-1.64375,-1.654336],[-1.6,-1.84],[-1.55625,-2.021836],[-1.5125,-2.199844],[-1.46875,-2.374023],[-1.425,-2.544375],[-1.38125,-2.710898],[-1.3375,-2.873594],[-1.29375,-3.032461],[-1.25,-3.1875],[-1.20625,-3.338711],[-1.1625,-3.486094],[-1.11875,-3.629648],[-1.075,-3.769375],[-1.03125,-3.905273],[-0.9875,-4.037344],[-0.94375,-4.165586],[-0.9,-4.29],[-0.85625,-4.410586],[-0.8125,-4.527344],[-0.76875,-4.640273],[-0.725,-4.749375],[-0.68125,-4.854648],[-0.6375,-4.956094],[-0.59375,-5.053711],[-0.55,-5.1475],[-0.50625,-5.237461],[-0.4625,-5.323594],[-0.41875,-5.405898],[-0.375,-5.484375],[-0.33125,-5.559023]